      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm against forcibly changing a user's avatar without their explicit permission.\n\nVRChat protects personal expression, this is part of why it's against the Creator Guidelines to forcibly change a user's avatar in a world.\n\nIt's also inconsistent with how Avatar Performance Gating works for example, where the user wearing the disallowed avatar can still wear it locally, while everyone else will see their fallback.\n\nI think this idea would work a lot better if it followed that same logic, staying consistent with how Avatar Performance Gating works.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
